  "context_pill": "Amalgamation Depreciation Apportionment",
  "example_summary": "Calculation of depreciation for Sai Ltd. and Shirdi Ltd. post-amalgamation using the Fifth Proviso to Section 32(1).",
  "source_provision": "| Provision | Description | Statutory Basis |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Depreciation Deduction | Allowable on block of assets | Section 32(1) |\n| Amalgamation Apportionment | Apportioned based on days of use | Fifth Proviso to Section 32(1) |\n| WDV Calculation | WDV at start of year for block | Section 43(6) |\n\n\n> [!IMPORTANT] Rule for Apportionment: The aggregate depreciation allowable to the amalgamating company and the amalgamated company shall not exceed the deduction calculated at prescribed rates as if the amalgamation had not taken place.\n\n\n> [!NOTE] Usage Threshold: Assets put to use for less than 180 days in the previous year attract depreciation at 50% of the normal prescribed rate.\n\n\n- The transfer price of assets between amalgamating and amalgamated companies is irrelevant for computing depreciation eligibility.\n- Total depreciation for the block is calculated on the aggregate WDV and current year additions, irrespective of the transfer.",
